<quiz>
  <question type="category">
    <category>
      <text>$course$/Math for College Readiness/Units/Unit 03/Lesson 06/MCR_U03_L06_GuidedPractice</text>
    </category>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>MCR_U03_L06_GP_Q01</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> MCR_U03_L06_GP_Q01</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> Readiness Support Only - Extension of MLA.MCR.DL.9</p><p>A survey asks 30 students from one lunch table about the whole school. What is the main concern?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[sampling bias]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. One lunch table may not represent the whole school.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[causation]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[The issue is sample selection, not cause and effect.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[positive association]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[The question does not describe two related variables.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[residual error]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Residuals belong to model predictions, not sampling design.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>MCR_U03_L06_GP_Q02</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> MCR_U03_L06_GP_Q02</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> Readiness Support Only - Extension of MLA.MCR.DL.9</p><p>The population is all high school students in a district. Which sample is most representative?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[students from one honors class]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[One class may not represent all students.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[students randomly selected from all district high schools]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. Random selection across schools better represents the population.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[only students at a football game]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This convenience sample may exclude many students.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[only students who volunteer online]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Voluntary response can create bias.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>MCR_U03_L06_GP_Q03</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> MCR_U03_L06_GP_Q03</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> Readiness Support Only - Extension of MLA.MCR.DL.9</p><p>Which survey question is biased?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[What time does school start?]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This asks for factual information.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Which schedule do you prefer?]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This is more neutral than praising one option.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Do you agree that the excellent new schedule should stay?]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. The wording pushes a positive opinion before the person answers.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[How many minutes is lunch?]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This asks for a measurement, not an opinion.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>MCR_U03_L06_GP_Q04</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> MCR_U03_L06_GP_Q04</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> Readiness Support Only - Extension of MLA.MCR.DL.9</p><p>A sample is chosen because it is easy to reach. What type of sample is this?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[random sample]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[A random sample is selected by chance.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[representative sample]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Easy access does not guarantee representation.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[population]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[The population is the entire group, not the selected sample.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[convenience sample]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. A convenience sample is selected because it is easy to access.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>MCR_U03_L06_GP_Q05</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> MCR_U03_L06_GP_Q05</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> Readiness Support Only - Extension of MLA.MCR.DL.9</p><p>Why should conclusions from a biased sample be limited?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[bias always makes arithmetic impossible]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Calculations can be done, but conclusions may be misleading.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[the sample may not represent the population]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. If the sample is biased, the results may not generalize fairly.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[bias proves causation]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Bias does not prove cause and effect.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[the population disappears]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[The population still exists; the sample may not represent it.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
</quiz>